note bottom of F
  **Now wired**, on two counts: the processor
  narrows it to ProcessedField, and render
  walks it for reasons. It was amber here
  while neither reader existed.

  Has **no fields left**. Its children were
  ""Vec<Extracted<TransformationExtraction, ..>>"",
  and that type is deleted — it was never a
  node, it held the author's transformation
  expression, which is ""#[from]"".

  Refilled by the derive (#field/children).
end note

note bottom of Y
  **On the macro path at last.** A field's
  children are its ATTRIBUTES, so the chain runs
  field_names -> Struct -> Field -> here. The
  module-wide ""#![allow(dead_code)]"" is gone.
  (#field/children, #syntax/not-driven)

  A doc comment IS an attribute, so a
  non-grammar head extracts to an EMPTY child
  carrying no value and NO REASON — otherwise
  every documented field is an error, which it
  once was. (#heads-are-rustcs)

  RESOLUTION is still deliberately off this path:
  ""resolve"" exists for a stage that must inspect,
  and the compiler-checked path splices instead.
  Those items keep a NARROW allow naming that.
  (#syntax/resolution-is-deferred-not-dead)
end note

note bottom of P
  **Wired.** Concrete impls for both
  extractions, driven from lib.rs.

  Sharpest demonstration of why the source
  rides on the OUTPUT: FieldExtraction's value
  carries NOTHING, so everything ProcessedField
  knows comes from ""input.source()"". Unwrap
  between stages and there is nothing to
  process. (#processor/needs-the-source)
end note

note top of G
  **No panics on this path.** Every derive returns
  ""Result<Vec<syn::Item>>"", each item validated by
  ""parse2(..)?"" where it was built, so a malformed
  one names the generator instead of arriving in
  the author's crate. Zero ""unwrap"" / ""expect"" /
  ""parse_quote!"" remain in production code.
  (#derive/expansion-is-typed-items)
end note

note bottom of G
  **Wired.** An enum fails extraction and the
  impl is STILL emitted — same associated items,
  vacant. Not an empty stream: that would leave
  every use site reporting "no associated item
  named FIELDS" on top of the real error.
  (#generator/stub-is-not-empty)
end note

legend right
  |<#E8F4EA>| live and tested |
